Explanation:

We set up the Lagrange system $nabla T = lambda nabla g$, which gives $4x^3 = -2lambda x$ and $4y = lambda$. This yields two cases: $x = 0$ (giving point $(0, -3)$ with temperature 19) and $x^2 = -2y$ (giving points $(+- sqrt(2), -1)$ with temperature 7). The minimum temperature is 7.
